  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Reinforced Cooperation and Knowledge for Water Security in Latin America and the Caribbean</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project is aimed to improve water governance and management in LAC, through enhanced cooperation and enhanced institutional and human capacities with more opportunities for gender equality in decision-making. It will heighten the impact of the work of the Spanish Agency for International Development Cooperation (AECID), the Conference of Ibero-American Water Directors (CODIA) and UNESCO in LAC by combining strengths in complementary areas in terms of training courses and knowledge management components based on effective networking.</narrative>
  </description>
